---
import ReferenceLayout from '../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { dataPagesOn } from '../lib/data/shell-dist';
import { DATA_PAGES_REVIEWED } from '../lib/data/review';

// The economic data sections appear only when the data pages are built (DATA_PAGES=on; rule D5
// of src/lib/data/shell-dist.ts; owner brief T): the held build is this page as it was.
const dataOn = dataPagesOn(process.env);
const updated = dataOn ? DATA_PAGES_REVIEWED : '2026-11-16';
---
<ReferenceLayout
  title="Corrections"
  description="How to report an error on RadMage Finance, how corrections are handled, and the log of published corrections."
  lead="Accuracy matters more than speed. When something on RadMage Finance is wrong, it is corrected openly and the correction is recorded here."
  updated={updated}
>
  <h2>Report an error</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with the address of
    the page and what you believe is wrong. A link to a source helps. For a calculator, include
    the inputs you used and the result you expected.
  </p>

  <h2>How corrections are handled</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>The report is checked against primary sources, or, for a calculator, against the independent reference implementation.</li>
    <li>If the page is wrong, it is fixed and a dated correction note is added to it, saying what changed.</li>
    <li>Corrections that change a fact, a figure or a calculator result are listed below.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Small edits that do not change meaning, such as fixing a typo, are made without a note.
  </p>
  {dataOn && (
    <p>
      On the economic data pages, a value that a publisher revises is not a correction of ours:
      each dashboard lists those changes in its log of the changes we observed between our
      collections. If
      RadMage Finance publishes data in error, the affected series return to an earlier snapshot
      and say that their updates are paused after a rollback, with the reason, and the correction
      is listed below.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Corrections log</h2>
  <p>No corrections have been published.</p>
</ReferenceLayout>
